{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 4a103ad5f073a9acda6bffcc3807def9294e8eb8 on builder/lv5-presence-20261121, all 29 artifacts, for request 401d09b4 under my promise d250d7fd. The implementation is LV5 (request f5b39d57, promise cbd0a018). The reporting artifact is the LV5 note.\n\nThe head has 8 commits on origin main 446e2ab8. `git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main 4a103ad5` gives tree d61746ea, the head's own tree, so the head is a fast-forward of main. `check-commit-messages 446e2ab8..4a103ad5` checks 8 commits and flags none. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, `git diff --check` is clean, and no added line names a local path.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **The gate.** END c54a9291 passed on source 05bc393b (tree 15b6f502, 0 changed files, exit 0, 1,916.28 s). The review head differs from 05bc393b in the note alone, so the gated source is the reviewed source. `gate.txt` hashes to `ca9157f2…`. The failed first run is retained: `2026-11-21-lv5-gate/gate.txt` hashes to `01af58ff…` and stops at the commit-message check before any test stage.\n- **The note's hashes.** All 23 log, report, screenshot and gate hashes in the note's tables match the files under `2026-11-21-lv5-retry-gate/`.\n- **Scope.** The 29 artifacts filed at this head equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 446e2ab8 4a103ad5`. No path under `apps/` or `examples/` changes, so no signed application bytes change, as the request says.\n\n## Replay: the two openings and the forged third entry\n\n`verify.ts:1453-1457` rejects an entry after the live confirmation in replay mode, before the signature and dependency reads. It calls `liveActive`, the predicate that the fold uses at `fold.ts:84`, and it throws the fold's own sentence. Promise 9 holds: replay and the runtime share one function. A non-live definition, and the genesis entry before a definition exists, never reach the branch.\n\n`live-creation.test.ts` replays a live child's creation and confirmation as `consistent` with coverage of the child and its parent. It then appends a canonical third entry that names a foreign retained input, and the report is `mismatch` at seq 2. The named control (`replay-control-on-lv2-commands.txt`) disables exactly that predicate with `false \u0026\u0026`, and the test fails because the report is no longer `mismatch`. I read the command and the log. The control ran on the LV2 base c20e5315, where `verify.ts` has the same text around this line.\n\nIntegrity mode runs no `#replay` and folds no entry of any scope kind, because it trusts the recorded judgments (`verify.ts:1478-1480`). It therefore neither takes the early branch nor reaches the fold, for a live scope as for every other scope. That is integrity mode's existing contract, and the new `docs/scopes.md` sentence says \"Replay\", which names the mode that derives entries. I found no replay path that accepts a third entry.\n\n## B4: declared, authenticated, timed presence\n\n`bindApplicationViews` admits `presence` only when all of these hold:\n- the view is a carousel over a live definition with one non-final source state;\n- the member field is a non-null party and the focus field a non-null scope ref;\n- the expiry field is a non-null time value;\n- the acts are exactly enter, renew and leave, with no arguments, and `enter` takes only the focus field;\n- the open act carries the `none` guard that admits one active lease per member and focus, and renew and leave carry the signer-equals-member guard;\n- open sets the party from the signer and the focus from its field;\n- the lease value is one positive whole number of seconds, identical in open and renew;\n- leave ends in a final state, and a timed rule moves the same state to the same final state at the deadline;\n- two refresh intervals (`refresh / 500`) fit inside the lease.\n\nI read the binder's code against each of these. `unsafe-cadence` (refresh 15,001 against a 30 s lease) is rejected in the fixture test. `readApplicationViews` restricts presence to carousels and raises the act cap only to 3.\n\nThe service path is the part that matters for authority. The server owns the action: the browser receives opaque IDs (`presence-enter`, `-renew`, `-leave`) and no arguments. The focus is the mounted scope from the opener's selection, never a browser value. `#viewLiveAct` rechecks the installation, the scope, the generation, and then the presence viewer against the live session (`session.claims.key`, membership and member). It requires that the viewer's own row, selected by member and focus, matches the displayed row id and revision for renew and leave, and that no own row exists for enter. The scope still judges every act itself. The `none` guard makes duplicate entry impossible even if two tabs race past the advisory check.\n\n`session.ts` now clears `liveDispatches` on every cut change. `liveAct` checks `#admit(instance, cut)` before it reads the retained outcomes, so an outcome from an old cut was already unreachable. The clear only frees memory under the 32-outcome bound.\n\nThe Chromium witness uses the production generated kit with a scripted host. It checks the member text (\"here\" for the mounted scope, the scope ID for another), the exact view and cut on enter, renew and leave, and that no further live act goes out for 60 s of fake time after teardown. Its `waitForFunction` predicates are all synchronous reads of `proof`, so the NF-7 failure (a Promise predicate that passes at once) does not apply. The installed native witness runs MCP, scope storage, the issued session and the live turn. It enters, renews, leaves, enters again, then fires the real timer after 30,001 ms. The lease ends in state `left`, the tick advances by one, and the journal keeps its 2 creation entries. The note states that these two witnesses are scripted-host and native-fixture boundaries, and the planner approved them.\n\n## Kernel changes, `docs/kernel.md` section 7\n\nThe sentences added to promises 1, 7 and 11 match section 4.3 of the live note word for word. Ruling `4b5e0ec2` permits them: its review names the fold's refusal of a later entry, and it names promises 1, 7 and 11 as the three that gain a sentence. The replay change is that refusal applied before dependency reads, and it adds no entry kind, scope kind, field type, capability or reason code. Promises 2, 4, 5, 8 and 10 keep their text, as section 4.3 says. The one-channel audit gains class E and its rows, and its D18 entry now says what was built.\n\n## Inherited subject exception\n\n`exceptInheritedSubject` accepts a flagged row only when its full 40-character ID is `446e2ab8…`, it has exactly one issue, and that issue is line 1, rule `subject-length`, length 185. It applies to the ordinary `BASE HEAD` range report alone. `--subjects-since`, `checkMessage` and the Git hook stay as they were, and the accepted finding prints on stdout. The test keeps both findings when the same commit has a second issue, keeps a neighbor with an identical length finding, and keeps a length of 186. The audit log and `direct-check.log` still show the original finding, and the original failed gate is retained. This matches proposal `0bfc78e2` and ratification `b9d87de3`.\n\n## Wake rate\n\nThe head adds no alarm and no DO schedule. It adds a client-driven renew:\n- **Floor:** 0 requests per hour with no open presence view.\n- **Per open view:** one projection read and one live act every `refresh`. A declared refresh runs from 1 s to 60 s, so each open view costs between 60 and 3,600 reads plus the same number of acts per hour. The fixture uses 2 s, which is 1,800 of each.\n- **What it touches:** the live scope's in-memory state and its one in-memory timer. The acts write no journal entry or storage row, and the journal stays at 2 entries.\n- **When it stops:** at teardown, at page hide, or when the host drops the page.\n\nA package author sets the cadence, and the head ships no authored package, so no deployed room gains this rate yet.\n\n## Non-blocking\n\n- `docs/kernel.md` section 7 still says of the live level, \"The level is designed and not built.\" LV2 to LV5 built it, and the roadmap and `docs/scopes.md` in this head say so. Change the sentence the next time that page changes. The same paragraph's sequenced sentence stays true.\n- The inherited-subject exception cannot trigger on a range whose base is 446e2ab8 or later, so it only matters to branches cut before main published that merge. Remove it once none remain.\n- A failed `enter` retries on every refresh. The cost is one signed act per interval per failing view, bounded by the refresh floor. Consider a back-off if a package author reports it.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The level adds no entry kind. Replay and the runtime share `liveActive`. Presence is a declared binding that the platform checks, not a new mechanism in the scope.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The browser holds no authority and no action arguments, the server rechecks viewer, row, generation and cut at act time, and the scope's own guards make the lease unique and tied to the signer.\n\nSafety: no finding. A lost leave cannot leave a lease behind, because the timed rule expires it. The native witness shows that rule firing, and the Chromium witness shows no live act after teardown. The scope keeps the two creation entries throughout.\n\nLiveness: no finding. Renewal runs on each refresh inside the validated lease window (two intervals fit), teardown ends the lease early on a best-effort basis, and the timer ends any lease that the view abandons. The cases that cannot renew (a stale cut, a changed viewer, a reset generation) fail visibly and recover on the next read.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c82061446e1ac5796f335f9523a6c95816d229c0","binding":"assigned","head":"4a103ad5f073a9acda6bffcc3807def9294e8eb8","head_news_acknowledged"